# cuts/v1.0.33/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.33. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.33 and by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND HOW ITS ABSENCE WAS FOUND
#
# A cut record is TWO files, not one. I wrote cut-manifests/v1.0.33.yaml and
# stopped, having read "the cut record for this version must exist" and treated
# the manifest as the whole of it. ORM had named both files; I actioned one.
#
# The DRY RUN caught it, which is exactly what the dry run is for. It cleared
# the manifest check and died one step later:
#
#     The cut record's CM051 pin is the tree being cut
#     CANNOT-RUN: no cuts/v1.0.33/cut.env
#     exit 2
#
# preflight red, cut job SKIPPED, dry-run job SKIPPED, and NO VERSION NUMBER
# SPENT. Discovering this on a tag push would have burnt v1.0.33 the way
# v1.0.27 through v1.0.31 were burnt.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TRAP THIS FILE IS THE THIRD DOCUMENTED VICTIM OF
#
# v1.0.31 pinned CM051=f219eb0f and instructed a human, in prose, to re-verify
# the install.sh blob immediately before tagging. The instruction was correct
# and was not executed. Three commits touched install.sh afterwards, the pin
# went dead, and cutting from it would have shipped the crash-looping Hub that
# v1.0.31 existed to fix. Prose cannot fail closed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PIN BELOW IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
#
# CM051 names main as of this file's creation. The blob was compared, not
# assumed, and the merge that immediately precedes it (#782, the cut record and
# the provenance rows) touches NO install.sh path:
#
#     CM051 pin 8d080862  install.sh blob  4414653df778acb26cc4feb5798697f0275c58e0
#     origin/main         install.sh blob  4414653df778acb26cc4feb5798697f0275c58e0
#     install.sh paths in the 8d080862 diff:  0   (measured, not inferred)
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSHING THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE, NOT
# BEFORE IT. TNM's #417 and #418 are open against vendor/ostler_fda and the
# vendor:ostler_fda hold is still RED; if either lands and touches install.sh,
# this pin goes dead the moment it merges:
#
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh
#
# If they diverge, re-point CM051 to main and re-run. A pin chosen early and
# trusted is the fifth thing to burn a tag in this series.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.58, signed, notarised and stapled. This is the
# DEREFERENCED commit: the tag is ANNOTATED, its tag object is 87cd9d9e, and
# recording that would pin the cut to a tag object rather than to source.
DAEMON_COMMIT=5b7efb00a541

# The CM051 tree whose install.sh ships in the DMG. See the blob note above.
CM051=8d08086297c0f6cd0a3b6c1cbd853e6f093e8563
